Comment (internal/service/relational/agent_config.go:37):
**Medium** · security

`BeforeDelete` blocks every GORM delete of revisions, and deleting an agent keeps them (`DeleteInstancesForAgent`: "Revisions are kept"). Combined with overlays being returned unredacted, a secret saved by mistake can't be removed through the app, even by deleting the agent, short of manual SQL.

Suggested fix: add a purge path — e.g. delete revisions in the `DeleteAgent` transaction (`Session(&gorm.Session{SkipHooks: true})` or raw SQL) and/or an admin action that redacts a revision's overlay in place.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Add a purge path: delete the agent config revisions when the agent is deleted. In the DeleteAgent flow (internal/api/handler/agents.go and agentcfg, e.g. a DeleteRevisionsForAgent next to DeleteInstancesForAgent), inside the same transaction, delete ccf_agent_config_revisions rows for the agent bypassing the append-only BeforeDelete hook (tx.Session(&gorm.Session{SkipHooks: true}) or a raw DELETE). Keep BeforeDelete for every other path. Fix the "Revisions are kept" comment and docs. Integration test: deleting an agent removes its revisions. In-place redaction of one revision is a follow-up; mention it in the PR body.

