Comment (internal/api/handler/agent_config_sync.go:164):
**Medium** · security

Only `base` and `effective` go through `RedactDocument`. `error` (up to 8 KiB), `warnings[].message`, `plugins[].source` and `remote-config` are stored and returned verbatim to every `agent:read` holder. Agent errors often embed connection strings or download URLs with tokens (e.g. `dial postgres://app:hunter2@db…`).

Suggested fix: run these free-text fields through the content check and replace a whole string with `MaskedValue` when `containsSecretValue` matches (after fixing the quadratic scan).
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** In PutReport (agent_config_sync.go), after normalizeReport, scrub free-text fields with the content check: report.Error, each warnings[].Message, each plugins[].Source -> replaced whole with agentconfig.MaskedValue when they contain a secret value; and the string leaves of report.RemoteConfig. Add an exported helper in pkg/agentconfig (e.g. ScrubSecretText(s string) (string, bool)) built on containsSecretValue (after the quadratic fix) instead of duplicating logic. Warn once per report when something was scrubbed, like the existing re-redaction warning. Unit tests for the helper plus a handler test.

