Comment (internal/authz/builtin.go:59):
**Low** · security (parity)

The builtin PDP allows agent subjects every action on `agent`, including `configure` and `read`. Not reachable today (admin routes use `JWTMiddleware`, which rejects agent tokens), but it's a gap vs Cedar, which grants agents only register/ingest/sync. A future agent-token route behind the agent guard would let one agent configure another.

Suggestion: allow only `ActionRegister`, `ActionIngest` and `ActionSync` when `s.Type == "agent"`.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** In internal/authz/builtin.go, for s.Type == "agent" allow only ActionRegister, ActionIngest and ActionSync on the agent resource (parity with Cedar); deny others with a clear Reason. Make sure the registration/ingest/sync routes still pass (unit + authz integration tests) and add a test that an agent subject is denied configure and read.

