Comment (pkg/agentconfig/validate.go:178):
**Low** · bug

O6 (plugin-name pattern) is applied to every plugin key in the overlay, not only plugins the overlay adds. `ValidateOverlay` has no base, so an overlay touching a file plugin whose name starts with `_`/`-` or is over 63 chars is always rejected, e.g. `{"plugins":{"_legacy":{"enabled":false}}}` → 422.

Suggestion: enforce the pattern only for names not in the base (base-aware step), or document the stricter rule.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Per the lisa rule (change OR document -> document): keep the check in ValidateOverlay and document the stricter rule: O6 applies to every plugin key in an overlay, so file plugins whose names do not match PluginNamePattern cannot be changed remotely. Update the ValidateOverlay / O6 doc comment, the PUT swag description if it lists rules, and docs describing overlay rules. No behaviour change.

