Comment (internal/service/relational/agentcfg/service.go:353):
**Low** · perf

Once the cap is reached, every digest-carrying heartbeat from an unregistered instance runs the UPDATE (0 rows), then `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` on the agent row, a `COUNT(*)` and a Warn log line — every beat, for every such instance. That contends with `CreateRevision` and floods logs. Suggestion: rate-limit the log and cache "cap reached" per agent for a short TTL.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** In agentcfg.Service remember "cap reached" per agent for a short TTL (e.g. 1 minute; map[uuid.UUID]time.Time guarded by a mutex). In TouchFromHeartbeat, when the UPDATE affected no row and the agent is within the TTL, skip the insert path (no FOR UPDATE / COUNT) and return nil. Set the entry when upsert returns ErrInstanceLimit (heartbeat and report paths); clear it when an insert succeeds. Log the Warn at most once per agent per TTL. UpsertReport keeps returning ErrInstanceLimit (409). Tests using the injectable clock (SetClock).

