Comment (pkg/agentconfig/sensitive.go:178):
**Low** · security

Some redaction gaps (checked with a scratch test):
- `https://user:5678/abc@host` isn't detected: `url.Parse` succeeds (reads `user:5678` as host:port), and the `continue` skips the regex fallback;
- scheme-less DSNs like `user:hunter2@tcp(db:3306)/app` under a non-secret key aren't detected;
- `plugins.*.source`, `policies` and `labels` are never content-checked, so `https://u:pw@…` in `source` survives `Redact`/`RedactDocument`.

Suggestion: always try `urlUserinfoPattern` too instead of skipping it when parse succeeds, and run the content check on sources/policies. (Regexes are RE2, so no ReDoS — the cost issue is the quadratic scan above.)
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** In sensitive.go hasURLPassword: when url.Parse succeeds but yields no password, still try urlUserinfoPattern on the candidate (do not continue past it), so https://user:5678/abc@host is caught. Add a scheme-less MySQL DSN pattern (user:pass@tcp(host:port)/db). In Redact and RedactDocument, also run the value content check (not the key rule) on plugins.*.source and plugins.*.policies[] strings, masking them when they contain a secret value. Tests for each case; keep regexes RE2/linear.

