Comment (internal/api/handler/agent_config_sync.go:197):
**Low** · bug

Postgres rejects `\^@` in jsonb and NUL bytes in text columns. A NUL in an overlay value, a report base/effective string or a hostname passes validation and then fails on INSERT, giving a 500 instead of a 4xx. Suggestion: reject NUL in `ValidateOverlay` and `normalizeReport`.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Reject NUL. In ValidateOverlay, walk every string (keys and values) and report FieldCodeInvalidValue at the pointer when it contains a NUL character. In normalizeReport, return a 400 if hostname, agent-version, error, effective-digest, warning messages or plugin fields contain NUL, or if the base/effective/remote-config raw JSON contains the \^@ escape (check the raw bytes for that six-character escape as well as decoded strings). Tests.

